{
  "id": "holt-shared-predator-fifth-systems",
  "name": "Shared-predator apparent competition between independent prey",
  "description": "Original illustrative normalized-density implementation of Holt1977 equations8-9 page204. Two prey have separate logistic resource bases and share a food-limited predator; no direct interspecific competition. Densities are divided by fixed reference densities, so capacities and conversion/nutritional coefficients use the same normalized convention. Nonnegative parameters and initial densities, positive capacities, time in days. Original defaults, no empirical fit. No adaptive diet, handling-time saturation, spatial structure, stochastic extinction or positivity clamp. Solver/step changes can break numerical positivity.",
  "category": "ecology",
  "source": "https://people.clas.ufl.edu/rdholt/files/001.pdf",
  "reference": "Holt,R.D.(1977). Predation, apparent competition, and the structure of prey communities. Theoretical Population Biology12:197-229. doi:10.1016/0040-5809(77)90042-9. Original authored equations/JSON; no paper text/figures/code copied.",
